# Project-level .opencode/ state and cache (gitignored, ephemeral)
#
# The **/ prefix is load-bearing. A pattern with an interior slash is anchored to
# the .gitignore's own directory, so a bare `.opencode/state/` matches the repo
# root only — and `veclib` resolves its store from process.cwd(), so running the
# vector tests (or any script) from a subdirectory silently created a 2 MB
# `.opencode/state/vector/code.db` that then showed up as untracked.
.opencode/state/
.opencode/cache/
**/.opencode/state/
**/.opencode/cache/
# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
